  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": -2,
  "section_notes": "S1 imposes strict 24-hour reporting for all incidents and 48-hour customer notice. S2 keeps the 55 °C test and 5% threshold but only triggers corrective action rather than an automatic sales stop, while giving per-model failure rates to customers and regulators but not the public. S3 requires new-unit shut-off and a 6-year retrofit with alternatives; S4 requires built-in suppression at 36 months; S5 mandates recall above 8/100k with prompt notices."
